{
	title: 'Configurable spawn budget, shown as bN',
	spec: 'Spawn slots for a new top-level session come from the config.ason setting subagentSlots (integer, min 0, default 3), stored when the session is created; sessions without a stored count fall back to the setting, with no compatibility code. Spawning a subagent (any mode, including fork) costs 1 slot from the spawner and from every ancestor up the owner chain, and is refused if any of them has 0 left. SPAWN limit sets the child’s own budget, at most the spawner’s remaining slots minus 1, and is not paid upfront: siblings may together be promised more than the spawner has, and whoever spends first gets the slots. /fork copies the remaining slots and starts its own tree. A model-spawned interactive tab is free and starts with subagentSlots, like a new tab. /budget N in any tab changes only that session’s count; ancestors still limit what it can spend. Models may read bare /budget; only the user changes it. Terminal, web and mobile always show the session’s slots left as bN (e.g. b3) next to the model name, linking to an explanation of the spawn budget and /budget, and updating live. Models may run /fork: a fork shares its parent’s context and gives no unbounded working space.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Each noninteractive spawn validates the full owner chain before creation, then decrements each count by one and pushes metadata. The child limit is not prepaid; interactive spawns have no owner and use the configured count. Session metadata validates stored slots; snapshots supply the configured fallback without writing old records. Both status rows keep bN beside the model and link /budget; narrow terminal rows prioritize model and count. Web uses a sibling native budget link over the existing details target rather than invalid nested interactive elements. Focused feature tests and rendered compact-status checks cover live updates at 320, 390, 1024 and 1600px.',
		'The shared host.broadcast boundary supplies effective configured slots on every metadata event, keeping legacy sessions without a stored count consistent across local terminal, remote terminal and web without persisting a compatibility migration.'
	],
	needs: ['t0', 'pc'],
	foldInto: ['t0']
}
